<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>When darkness doth Thy face obscure,</l><l>And many sorrows I endure,</l><l>I think of Christ’s Gethsemane;</l><l>Thy will is mine, whate’er it be.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>When tender joys to me are known,</l><l>I render thanks to Thee alone;</l><l>I know my cup is filled by Thee;</l><l>Thy will is mine, whate’er it be.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Thus calmly do I face my lot,</l><l>Accept it, Lord, and doubt Thee not;</l><l>Lo! all things work for good to me;</l><l>Thy will is mine, whate’er it be.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
